  [1mEXPORT-ALL-APPLICATIONS[0m

  Export all applications in a workspace

  Usage:

    [33mexport-all-applications[0m|[33mexaa[0m {OPTIONS}

  Options:

    [33m-workspaceid[0m|[33m-woi[0m <workspaceid> {INTEGER} [required]
    Workspace ID for which all applications to be exported or the workspace to
    be exported

    [33m-exptype[0m|[33m-exty[0m <exptype>
    {APEXLANG|APPLICATION_SOURCE|CHECKSUM-SH1|CHECKSUM-SH256|EMBEDDED_CODE|READABLE_JSON|READABLE_YAML|SQL,...}
    (APPLICATION_SOURCE)
    Comma delimited list of export types to perform: 
    * APPLICATION_SOURCE: Export an APEX application using other parameters
    passed.
    * APEXLANG: Export a readable version of the application meta-data in
    APEXlang format.
    * SQL: Export am APEX application in to SQL format.
    * EMBEDDED_CODE: Export code such as SQL, PL/SQL and Javascript. APEX
    ignores all other options when EMBEDDED_CODE is selected.
    * CHECKSUM-SH1: Export a SHA1 checksum that is independent of IDs and can be
    compared across instances and workspaces.
    * CHECKSUM-SH256: Export a SHA-256 checksum that is independent of IDs and
    can be compared across instances and workspaces.
    * READABLE_JSON: Export a readable version of the application meta-data in
    JSON format.
    * READABLE_YAML: Export a readable version of the application meta-data in
    YAML format.
    On APEX version 26.1 and after readable formats will be exported as
    APEXlang.

    [33m-split[0m|[33m-sp[0m
    Split applications into multiple files

    [33m-skipexportdate[0m|[33m-sked[0m
    Skip export date in application export files

    [33m-exppubreports[0m|[33m-exre[0m
    Export all user saved public interactive reports 

    [33m-expsavedreports[0m|[33m-exsr[0m
    Export all user saved interactive reports 

    [33m-expirnotif[0m|[33m-exir[0m
    Export all interactive report notifications 

    [33m-exptranslations[0m|[33m-extr[0m
    Export the translation mappings and all text from the translation repository
    

    [33m-exporiginalids[0m|[33m-exoi[0m
    Causes export to emit ids as they are in the system

    [33m-expnosubscriptions[0m|[33m-exns[0m
    Do not export references to subscribed components 

    [33m-expcomments[0m|[33m-exco[0m
    Export developer comments. Deprecated for APEX 26.1 or higher since comments
    are included in export by default. Use DISABLE-EXP-COMMENTS option to omit
    them.

    [33m-disable-exp-comments[0m|[33m-dexc[0m
    Disable comments in export in APEX 26.1 on higher. Use EXPCOMMENTS option on
    earlier APEX versions.

    [33m-expsupportingobjects[0m|[33m-exso[0m <expsupportingobjects> {I|N|Y} (Y)
    Pass (Y)es, (N)o or (I)nstall to override the default 

    [33m-exitwhendone[0m|[33m-exwd[0m
    When true will cause SqlCl to exit upon completion of command.

    [33m-expaclassignments[0m|[33m-exacl[0m
    Export ACL User Role Assignments 

    [33m-debug[0m|[33m-de[0m
    Enable Debug output

    [33m-expcomponents[0m|[33m-exc[0m <expcomponents>
    Export application components. Parameters must be of form TYPE:ID, multiple
    values must be quoted "TYPE:ID TYPE:ID" 

    [33m-overwrite-files[0m|[33m-ovf[0m
    Overwrite any files produced by this process if they already exist

    [33m-expruntimeinstances[0m|[33m-exrin[0m <expruntimeinstances> {TASK|WORKFLOW,...} (NULL)
    Comma separated list for which to export runtime instance data.
    * WORKFLOW: Export workflow instances and task instances associated to a
    workflow.
    * TASK: Export task instances not associated to any workflow.

    [33m-force[0m|[33m-f[0m
    If the directory and files already exist in creation location, providing
