  [1mVALIDATE[0m

  Validates that the APEXlang input can be compiled. When no input path is
  provided, defaults to using current directory.

  Usage:

    [33mvalidate[0m|[33mval[0m {OPTIONS}

  Options:

    [33m-input[0m|[33m-i[0m <input>
    The path to the APEXlang input to validate. Input must be a path to a
    directory, zip or APEXlang file. APEXlang file input must define the full
    APEX application.

    [33m-workspaceid[0m|[33m-woi[0m <workspaceid> {INTEGER}
    The workspace id used for the validation process if multiple workspaces are
    available with current connection.

    [33m-workspace[0m|[33m-ws[0m <workspace>
    The workspace name used for generate, validate or import commands if
    multiple workspaces are available with current connection. If workspace id
    option is also provided, that value will be used instead of this option.

    [33m-deployment[0m|[33m-d[0m <deployment>
    Specify the path to the deployment file to use for import.

    [33m-debug[0m|[33m-de[0m
    Enable Debug output

  Examples:

    Validate current directory.
      [33mSQL> apex validate[0m
    
    Validate directory.
      [33mSQL> apex validate -input ./projects/brookstrut[0m
    
    Validate zip file
      [33mSQL> apex validate -input ./brookstrut.zip[0m
    
    Validate APEXlang file.
      [33mSQL> apex validate -input ./application.apx[0m
    
    Validate with specific workspace id.
      [33mSQL> apex validate -input ./projects/brookstrut -workspaceid 90000[0m
    


  [1mIMPORT[0m

  Imports the APEXlang input using current connection. When no input path is
  provided, defaults to using current directory.

  Usage:

    [33mimport[0m|[33mimp[0m {OPTIONS}

  Options:

    [33m-input[0m|[33m-i[0m <input>
    The path to the APEXlang input to be imported. Can be directory, zip file or
    single APEXlang file containing the entire app.

    [33m-workspaceid[0m|[33m-woi[0m <workspaceid> {INTEGER}
    The workspace id used for the import process if multiple workspaces are
    available with current connection.

    [33m-workspace[0m|[33m-ws[0m <workspace>
    The workspace name used for generate, validate or import commands if
    multiple workspaces are available with current connection. If workspace id
    option is also provided, that value will be used instead of this option.

    [33m-id[0m|[33m-id[0m <id> {INTEGER}
    Override the application id in the APEXlang input that the APEX application
    will use on import.

    [33m-schema[0m|[33m-sch[0m <schema>
    Override the application schema in the APEXlang input that the APEX
    application will use on import.

    [33m-name[0m|[33m-n[0m <name>
    Override the application name in the APEXlang input that the APEX
    application will use on import.

    [33m-alias[0m|[33m-al[0m <alias>
    Override the alias in the APEXlang input that the APEX application will use
    on import.

    [33m-image-prefix[0m|[33m-impr[0m <image-prefix>
    Override the image prefix in the APEXlang input that the APEX application
    will use on import.

    [33m-proxy[0m|[33m-pr[0m <proxy>
    Override the application proxy in the APEXlang input that the APEX
    application will use on import.

    [33m-deployment[0m|[33m-d[0m <deployment>
    Specify the path to the deployment file to use for import.

    [33m-debug[0m|[33m-de[0m
    Enable Debug output

  Examples:

    Import current directory.
      [33mSQL> apex import[0m
    
    Import directory.
      [33mSQL> apex import -input ./projects/brookstrut[0m
    
    Import zip file
      [33mSQL> apex import -input ./brookstrut.zip[0m
    
    Import APEXlang file.
      [33mSQL> apex import -input ./application.apx[0m
    
    Import under different application id.
      [33mSQL> apex import -input ./projects/brookstrut -id 1001[0m
    
    Import with specific workspace id.
      [33mSQL> apex import -input ./projects/brookstrut -workspaceid 90000[0m
    

Examples:

  Export an application with the application id is 1234.
    [33mSQL> apex export -applicationid 1234[0m
  
  Export all applications in the workspace with id is 1908816359534887.
    [33mSQL> apex export -workspaceid 1908816359534887[0m
  
  To export an application as a directory with each application component split
  into a separate file, use the apex export command and include the application
  ID and the -split option.
    [33mSQL> apex export -applicationid 1234 -split[0m
  
  To export an application in APEXlang format, use the apex export command,
  include the application ID and set -exptype to APEXLANG.
    [33mSQL> apex export -applicationid 1234 -exptype APEXLANG[0m
  
  Lists applications installed in the database.
    [33mSQL> apex list[0m
  Reports APEX application usage from APEX_WORKSPACE_LOG_SUMMARY.
    [33mSQL> apex log[0m 
